1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,494
Let me walk you through this loan default risk dashboard.

2
00:00:03,654 --> 00:00:08,862
It brings applicant assessment, predictions, and model
explanations together in one place.

3
00:00:09,717 --> 00:00:13,690
We start with the analytics dashboard for a quick view of
the applicant pool.

4
00:00:13,850 --> 00:00:18,779
The charts show repayment outcomes and how applicants are
distributed across different groups.

5
00:00:19,650 --> 00:00:23,814
To assess an applicant, we enter their annual income and
loan amount.

6
00:00:23,974 --> 00:00:28,852
The form also includes optional details, like the loan
annuity and goods price.

7
00:00:29,717 --> 00:00:35,965
Next, we complete the applicant profile, including age,
employment, family details, and housing.

8
00:00:36,125 --> 00:00:39,784
I've shortened the data entry here so we can focus on the
workflow.

9
00:00:40,650 --> 00:00:44,854
External credit scores can be added when available, or
left blank.

10
00:00:45,014 --> 00:00:49,467
Once the details are ready, we select Assess risk to
generate the estimate.

11
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:55,373
For this example, the estimated default probability is
seven point six percent.

12
00:00:55,533 --> 00:01:00,132
The dashboard shows a risk score of eight out of one
hundred, in the low risk band.

13
00:01:00,983 --> 00:01:06,022
This is an analytical estimate, not a guaranteed outcome
or an automatic lending decision.

14
00:01:06,182 --> 00:01:08,566
The result still needs human review.

15
00:01:09,417 --> 00:01:14,100
The explainability page shows which features are
associated with the model's predictions.

16
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:19,349
It also includes an applicant level breakdown to help us
understand this particular result.

17
00:01:20,217 --> 00:01:24,045
Model Selection compares the candidates using cross
validation.

18
00:01:24,205 --> 00:01:30,304
Here, XGBoost is selected, with the comparison results and
tuning details available for review.

19
00:01:31,183 --> 00:01:36,377
The performance page brings together test metrics,
threshold analysis, and calibration.

20
00:01:36,537 --> 00:01:40,805
These views help us examine how the model behaves beyond a
single prediction.

21
00:01:41,683 --> 00:01:46,577
For more detail, the methodology pages explain the
formulas behind the scores.

22
00:01:46,737 --> 00:01:52,065
The feature reference documents the inputs, derived
features, and how missing values are handled.

23
00:01:52,917 --> 00:01:57,590
Finally, Model Information records the model version and
training details.

24
00:01:57,750 --> 00:02:02,879
Together, these pages make the assessment easier to
inspect, explain, and review.
